{
  "about": "The original Lords of the Realm II's features, in a player's words, each graded against our engine on main. The player's page (node tools/pm/work.js --html) is drawn from this file. Rules: (1) grade from evidence, never from memory - 'done' cites a correction (C123), a test or file path, or an inventory entry (arms:<id or group>, audio:<id or class>), and work.js --check proves every citation exists on main; (2) 'partial' says in a few words what is missing, in gap, and names the docs/work.json rows that cover it; (3) 'missing' names its row where there is one - a missing or partial feature with no row is reported by --check as work nobody has written down; (4) 'not-assessed' is always better than a guess; (5) when a cited row merges it leaves the ledger and --check fails here: re-grade the feature and cite what landed. One feature per line; names are a few words.",
  "statuses": {
    "done": "the original's behaviour is built and checked; evidence cites what shows it",
    "partial": "built, with a named gap; gap says what is missing and rows name the work that covers it",
    "missing": "the original has it and we do not",
    "not-assessed": "nobody has checked, so no grade is claimed",
    "out-of-scope": "deliberately outside the current goal"
  },
